READ: AUC is invariant to affine, gamma, histogram matching - every monotone correction.
AUC ~0.5 in a year means GRVI carries NO canopy information there and IR-MAD cannot help.
AUC high but a shifted mean means it is purely a CALIBRATION problem, which IS fixable.
"separation" is the canopy-vs-other GRVI gap in standard deviations - a scale-free effect size.
